     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, at some frequency.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
