     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I'm sorry I said I would. I shouldn't have offered that before thinking it through.\n\nThe reason you gave, getting everything settled before the family visit and evening rounds, is about timing. It isn't a clinical reason for a dose twice the labeled maximum. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis and serious GI toxicity is real, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove it.\n\nHere are some ways to get this done today:\n- **I can enter metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum). You can titrate later if needed.\n- **I can enter a lower starting dose**, such as 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg daily, if the patient is starting metformin.\n- **If you think this patient needs a dose above the maximum**, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can place or co-sign the order through their own process. I can add a note to the order referencing that discussion.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
